WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.234
-Donald Trump has endorsed

00:00:03.234 --> 00:00:04.734
one of the most pro-MAGA
members of the Republican Party,

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:06.667
Ohio congressman Jim Jordan,

00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:08.033
to be the next
Speaker of the House,

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:09.868
which could put one of
the most prominent supporters

00:00:09.868 --> 00:00:12.801
of the coup attempt on January
6th in charge of the chamber.

00:00:12.801 --> 00:00:14.701
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:14.701 --> 00:00:16.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.634 --> 00:00:21.267
When last we left
the House Republican caucus,

00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:22.968
several of them
were organizing an effort

00:00:22.968 --> 00:00:25.567
to draft Donald Trump himself
to be the next speaker,

00:00:25.567 --> 00:00:27.934
which is possible since
technically the speaker

00:00:27.934 --> 00:00:29.467
does not have to be
a member of Congress.

00:00:29.467 --> 00:00:31.701
Apparently, it doesn't even need
to be a sentient human being.

00:00:31.701 --> 00:00:35.601
It could be one of those air
dancers outside car dealerships.

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:37.000
Republicans would probably
love that

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.100
because it has the same
hand movements as Donald Trump.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:42.601
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.601 --> 00:00:44.300
And apparently Trump was serious

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.834
about at least considering
a bid to become speaker.

00:00:46.834 --> 00:00:48.467
Politico reported
last week that...

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:54.400
Should he even be allowed
back in the Capitol,

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.400
based on what happened
last time he was there?

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.601
I mean, I'm on a year ban
from Vrbo

00:00:58.601 --> 00:01:01.100
because some guy said
I rented his place,

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:02.267
after I rented his place,

00:01:02.267 --> 00:01:03.701
the Q went missing
from the Scrabble game.

00:01:03.701 --> 00:01:06.367
But Trump,
Trump foments an insurrection

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:09.133
and is allowed to come
and go as he pleases.

00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:11.367
Also, the Q
was already missing, dude.

00:01:11.367 --> 00:01:13.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:14.467
But I guess Trump
is allowed back.

00:01:14.467 --> 00:01:16.300
In fact, his best bud
Sean Hannity

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:18.934
claimed on air last week
that sources were telling him

00:01:18.934 --> 00:01:21.367
Trump was open to the idea
of becoming speaker.

00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:23.367
Now, again, keep in mind
as you watch this clip,

00:01:23.367 --> 00:01:26.133
Hannity isn't just a pundit
who interviews Trump.

00:01:26.133 --> 00:01:27.868
He's appeared onstage with Trump
at rallies,

00:01:27.868 --> 00:01:30.234
and during Trump's presidency,
the two reportedly talked

00:01:30.234 --> 00:01:32.267
on a near nightly basis
before bedtime.

00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:33.734
According to
"New York Magazine,"

00:01:33.734 --> 00:01:37.801
on the phone, Hannity and Trump
alternate between the witch hunt

00:01:37.801 --> 00:01:40.901
and gabbing like old girlfriends
about media and gossip

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:43.601
and whose show sucks and who's
getting killed in the ratings

00:01:43.601 --> 00:01:46.033
and who's winning and sports
and Kanye West,

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:47.567
all of it sprinkled

00:01:47.567 --> 00:01:51.834
with a staccato [bleep]
[bleep] [bleep] [bleep]

00:01:51.834 --> 00:01:54.400
So Trump and Hannity
aren't just media allies,

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:57.567
they're best buds,
which is context for this clip

00:01:57.567 --> 00:02:00.133
in which Hannity claims
sources were telling him

00:02:00.133 --> 00:02:02.033
Trump was open
to becoming speaker.

00:02:02.033 --> 00:02:03.968
-Sources telling me at this hour

00:02:03.968 --> 00:02:07.334
some House Republicans
have been in contact with

00:02:07.334 --> 00:02:08.868
and have started an effort

00:02:08.868 --> 00:02:11.300
to draft former president
Donald Trump

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:12.868
to be the next speaker.

00:02:12.868 --> 00:02:16.667
And I have been told
that President Trump

00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:19.300
might be open to helping
the Republican Party,

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:21.868
at least in the short term,
if necessary.

00:02:21.868 --> 00:02:22.968
-So the source was Trump.

00:02:22.968 --> 00:02:24.934
Whenever you hear

00:02:24.934 --> 00:02:27.734
Sean Hannity float something
like that on television,

00:02:27.734 --> 00:02:30.467
it's because it's something
Donald Trump told him to say

00:02:30.467 --> 00:02:32.234
or, at the very least, it's
something Trump wants to hear.

00:02:32.234 --> 00:02:34.100
At this point,
I wouldn't be surprised

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:36.601
if Trump was writing
the Fox News chyrons

00:02:36.601 --> 00:02:39.400
live in real time
via voice to text.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:50.834
And Trump himself
essentially confirmed

00:02:50.834 --> 00:02:51.968
the veracity of this report

00:02:51.968 --> 00:02:53.534
when he was asked
about the possibility

00:02:53.534 --> 00:02:54.901
of becoming speaker last week

00:02:54.901 --> 00:02:56.834
at his fraud trial
in a Manhattan court.

00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:06.033
-Would you take the job?

00:03:06.033 --> 00:03:07.567
Would you take the job?

00:03:09.767 --> 00:03:11.400
Would you take the job?

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:25.434
-Trump will always say
he's considering something

00:03:25.434 --> 00:03:26.801
when you first ask him about it.

00:03:26.801 --> 00:03:28.434
The reporter could stand up
at a press conference

00:03:28.434 --> 00:03:30.200
and say, "Mr. President,
sources are telling us

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:32.133
you're considering jumping
into the gorilla enclosure

00:03:32.133 --> 00:03:33.868
at the Bronx Zoo
and challenging the largest ape

00:03:33.868 --> 00:03:36.000
to a wrestling match
in order to subdue him,

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:38.200
claim his territory, and become
king of the primates."

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:40.667
And Trump would say, "We're
looking very strongly at it.

00:03:40.667 --> 00:03:44.234
I'm certainly -- I'm certainly
getting a lot of calls

00:03:44.234 --> 00:03:47.601
saying, 'You're the only one
who can defeat Mongo.'"

00:03:47.601 --> 00:03:51.100
But as random and insane
as this idea sounds,

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:52.634
it apparently did not
come out of nowhere.

00:03:52.634 --> 00:03:54.133
Over the weekend,
ABC News reported

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:56.067
that Trump actually maneuvered
behind the scenes

00:03:56.067 --> 00:03:57.801
to become Speaker of the House
back in January.

00:03:57.801 --> 00:03:59.701
And apparently the reason
he did that

00:03:59.701 --> 00:04:02.234
was because he was angry
he wasn't getting more votes

00:04:02.234 --> 00:04:03.634
during the initial
rounds of voting.

00:04:03.634 --> 00:04:05.801
-Sources tell ABC News
former president Trump

00:04:05.801 --> 00:04:09.334
secretly plotted to be elected
Speaker of the House in January

00:04:09.334 --> 00:04:10.901
while he was publicly supporting

00:04:10.901 --> 00:04:13.300
now-former speaker
Kevin McCarthy's bid.

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:14.501
-Publicly, Donald Trump

00:04:14.501 --> 00:04:17.334
had endorsed Kevin McCarthy
for speaker.

00:04:17.334 --> 00:04:22.033
But what I've learned is that
when Trump saw Matt Gaetz

00:04:22.033 --> 00:04:24.667
step up on the seventh ballot
back in January

00:04:24.667 --> 00:04:27.334
and vote for Donald Trump
for speaker

00:04:27.334 --> 00:04:30.033
and then he saw
all the cable networks,

00:04:30.033 --> 00:04:31.734
you know, relay the vote count

00:04:31.734 --> 00:04:33.834
and it was only
a single vote for Trump --

00:04:33.834 --> 00:04:36.667
you know, 212 votes
for Hakeem Jeffries,

00:04:36.667 --> 00:04:38.734
200 for Kevin McCarthy,

00:04:38.734 --> 00:04:40.367
some others had
a handful of votes,

00:04:40.367 --> 00:04:42.334
and then only one
for Donald Trump --

00:04:42.334 --> 00:04:46.234
Trump became angry
and he actually reached out,

00:04:46.234 --> 00:04:50.300
contacted Gaetz,
made his views known

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:53.434
within a small circle
of Republicans

00:04:53.434 --> 00:04:55.534
that the only reason
he only got one vote

00:04:55.534 --> 00:04:58.000
is that nobody bothered
to nominate him,

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:01.334
and so people didn't know
they could vote for him.

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:03.167
And at that point,
he made it clear

00:05:03.167 --> 00:05:06.200
that he wanted Matt Gaetz

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.734
to nominate him
for Speaker of the House.

00:05:08.734 --> 00:05:11.567
-Okay, so just to recap, Trump,
who was publicly supporting

00:05:11.567 --> 00:05:13.601
now-former speaker
Kevin McCarthy,

00:05:13.601 --> 00:05:16.634
but he was also mad
in the seventh round of voting

00:05:16.634 --> 00:05:18.167
he only got one vote
for speaker.

00:05:18.167 --> 00:05:19.567
I'm sure when he saw this,

00:05:19.567 --> 00:05:21.701
his text to Hannity
looked like this.

00:05:21.701 --> 00:05:24.400
[ Laughter ]

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:26.701
So Trump then asked
Congressman Matt Gaetz

00:05:26.701 --> 00:05:28.767
to officially
nominate him for speaker,

00:05:28.767 --> 00:05:31.133
assuming this meant the votes
would start pouring in for him.

00:05:31.133 --> 00:05:33.200
And Gaetz did that.
He stood up, made a big speech,

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:35.234
and nominated Donald Trump
to be Speaker of the House.

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:37.334
So what happened
after Gaetz nominated him?

00:05:37.334 --> 00:05:39.501
Did Trump get 100 votes
for speaker, 200 votes?

00:05:39.501 --> 00:05:40.868
How close did he come?

00:05:40.868 --> 00:05:43.868
-When that speech was over,
they called for the roll,

00:05:43.868 --> 00:05:46.534
and they once again
did another round of voting.

00:05:46.534 --> 00:05:49.000
And once again, Donald Trump
got a single vote

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:51.334
for Speaker of the House.

00:05:51.334 --> 00:05:52.667
-Did he call Gaetz again?

00:05:52.667 --> 00:05:54.434
[ As Trump ] I think this time
when you nominate me,

00:05:54.434 --> 00:05:58.167
say, "I'm being serious,
you guys.

00:05:58.167 --> 00:06:00.367
This isn't some dumb joke."

00:06:00.367 --> 00:06:02.200
[ Normal voice ] It was so bad,
that night on "Hannity,"

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:03.200
the chyron said...

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:13.701
So Trump's last attempt to get
votes for speaker went badly,

00:06:13.701 --> 00:06:16.200
which must be why
he's now abandoned

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:17.567
this latest bid for the job.

00:06:17.567 --> 00:06:20.033
Instead, he endorsed
far-right extremist Jim Jordan,

00:06:20.033 --> 00:06:23.267
perhaps the most pro-MAGA member
of the House GOP caucus

00:06:23.267 --> 00:06:24.634
and one of the key players

00:06:24.634 --> 00:06:26.801
in the attempt to overturn
the election on January 6th.

00:06:26.801 --> 00:06:28.167
You might remember
Jordan as the guy

00:06:28.167 --> 00:06:30.300
who would routinely show up
to hearings in the House

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:31.834
that were supposed
to be investigating

00:06:31.834 --> 00:06:34.667
the Trump administration,
but instead talk really fast

00:06:34.667 --> 00:06:36.968
and say totally incoherent
bull[bleep] like this.

00:06:36.968 --> 00:06:38.801
-James Comey, director, fired.

00:06:38.801 --> 00:06:41.567
Andy McCabe,
deputy director, fired,

00:06:41.567 --> 00:06:45.501
lied three times under oath,
under investigation as we speak.

00:06:45.501 --> 00:06:48.033
Jim Baker, FBI counsel, demoted,

00:06:48.033 --> 00:06:49.868
then left, currently
under investigation

00:06:49.868 --> 00:06:51.901
by the U.S. Attorney's Office
in Connecticut.

00:06:51.901 --> 00:06:53.567
Lisa Page demoted, then left.

00:06:53.567 --> 00:06:54.667
Ambassador Taylor recalls

00:06:54.667 --> 00:06:56.234
that Mr. Morrison
told Ambassador Taylor

00:06:56.234 --> 00:06:58.234
that I told Mr. Morrison
that I conveyed this message

00:06:58.234 --> 00:07:00.234
to Mr. Yermak
on September 1, 2019,

00:07:00.234 --> 00:07:01.634
in connection with
Vice President Pence's

00:07:01.634 --> 00:07:02.934
visit to Warsaw.

00:07:02.934 --> 00:07:05.200
-He sounds like an auctioneer
with a head injury,

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:08.133
just repeating
all the unhinged buzzwords

00:07:08.133 --> 00:07:10.100
you hear on Fox News
without any of the content.

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:11.701
It's like
if Thanksgiving dinner,

00:07:11.701 --> 00:07:14.601
everyone in your family
had a time limit to speak.

00:07:14.601 --> 00:07:16.400
"Uncle Jerry,
what are you thankful for?"

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:17.734
"Well, I guess I'm thankful
for my health

00:07:17.734 --> 00:07:19.701
and continued efforts
to stop trans, woke, Benghazi,

00:07:19.701 --> 00:07:22.968
Whitewater, China, laptop,
Hunter e-mails, tan suit."

00:07:22.968 --> 00:07:24.901
And it makes sense
that Jordan would spew

00:07:24.901 --> 00:07:27.501
random Fox News talking points,
because he is far and away

00:07:27.501 --> 00:07:29.767
the most popular Republican
congressman on Fox News.

00:07:29.767 --> 00:07:31.367
Since August 2017...

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:43.434
565 times.

00:07:43.434 --> 00:07:46.968
I don't even think
I've appeared on this show

00:07:46.968 --> 00:07:49.934
565 times since 2017.

00:07:49.934 --> 00:07:51.234
In fairness,
we did have that stretch

00:07:51.234 --> 00:07:53.100
where I was replaced
by a guest host.

00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:54.334
Who was that again?

00:07:54.334 --> 00:07:57.534
Oh, damn it!
He's everywhere.

00:07:57.534 --> 00:07:59.033
On the bright side,
it only took him

00:07:59.033 --> 00:08:01.033
about 90 seconds to get
through "A Closer Look."

00:08:01.033 --> 00:08:05.100
And when he does go on Fox News,
it won't surprise you to learn

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:06.300
he doesn't make
all that much sense,

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:07.934
like when he said this
over the weekend

00:08:07.934 --> 00:08:09.300
about his bid to become speaker.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:10.601
-The American people
right now, Maria,

00:08:10.601 --> 00:08:13.901
I think are -- they are
so thirsty for leadership.

00:08:13.901 --> 00:08:15.868
And I don't think they're seeing
it from the White House.

00:08:15.868 --> 00:08:17.501
I don't think they're
getting it from the Senate.

00:08:17.501 --> 00:08:19.267
They are hungry for leadership.

00:08:19.267 --> 00:08:20.667
-Oh, they're thirsty and hungry?

00:08:20.667 --> 00:08:22.734
"Maria, the American people
are thirsty for leadership.

00:08:22.734 --> 00:08:23.968
They're hungry for leadership.

00:08:23.968 --> 00:08:25.234
And dare I say,
they're horny for leadership.

00:08:25.234 --> 00:08:26.601
Don't take it from me.

00:08:26.601 --> 00:08:28.667
Take it from the audience
at the "Beetlejuice" musical."

00:08:28.667 --> 00:08:32.167
But by far, the most
dangerous thing about Jordan

00:08:32.167 --> 00:08:34.701
is that he was arguably
the most prominent supporter

00:08:34.701 --> 00:08:36.434
in Congress
of Donald Trump's attempt

00:08:36.434 --> 00:08:37.901
to overturn the 2020 election.

00:08:37.901 --> 00:08:39.501
He was intimately involved

00:08:39.501 --> 00:08:41.267
in the planning
of Trump's coup attempt,

00:08:41.267 --> 00:08:43.400
and has flat-out
refused requests

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:45.567
to provide more information
about his involvement.

00:08:45.567 --> 00:08:48.501
-Jim Jordan scored former
president Trump's endorsement

00:08:48.501 --> 00:08:51.267
early this morning, which
should come as no surprise.

00:08:51.267 --> 00:08:53.667
Here is Jordan in
Harrisburg, Pennsylvania,

00:08:53.667 --> 00:09:00.133
attending a Stop the Steal rally
two days after Election Day.

00:09:00.133 --> 00:09:02.000
In the weeks and months
after that,

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:05.067
Jordan went on various
right-wing media outlets

00:09:05.067 --> 00:09:09.767
where he attempted to sow
distrust in the 2020 election

00:09:09.767 --> 00:09:13.334
and made baseless claims
of election fraud.

00:09:13.334 --> 00:09:16.701
Jordan's name appears
throughout the bipartisan report

00:09:16.701 --> 00:09:19.100
from the House Select Committee
investigating January 6th.

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:20.601
The report says
that Jordan attended

00:09:20.601 --> 00:09:22.667
numerous post-election meetings

00:09:22.667 --> 00:09:25.267
with senior White House
officials and Rudy Giuliani

00:09:25.267 --> 00:09:27.767
discussing how to challenge
the election results.

00:09:27.767 --> 00:09:29.067
-I don't know what's
more shocking --

00:09:29.067 --> 00:09:30.934
that people still have meetings
with Rudy Giuliani

00:09:30.934 --> 00:09:32.801
or that Rudy Giuliani
made it to the meeting.

00:09:32.801 --> 00:09:35.734
When he was told
to meet with Jim Jordan,

00:09:35.734 --> 00:09:37.334
Rudy probably thought
he was meeting

00:09:37.334 --> 00:09:39.968
in a gymnasium
with Michael Jordan.

00:09:39.968 --> 00:09:41.033
[ As Giuliani ] Hey, Mike,
you've always been

00:09:41.033 --> 00:09:42.234
my favorite baseball player.

00:09:42.234 --> 00:09:43.834
Go, White Sox.

00:09:43.834 --> 00:09:45.200
[ Laughter ]

00:09:48.467 --> 00:09:49.868
[ Normal voice ]
A lot of time was spent today

00:09:49.868 --> 00:09:52.834
on, what would Rudy say
to Michael Jordan in a gym?

00:09:52.834 --> 00:09:54.567
[ Laughter ]

00:09:56.667 --> 00:09:59.200
Trump endorsing Jordan
is a perfect encapsulation

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:00.701
of where the GOP
is at right now.

00:10:00.701 --> 00:10:03.334
A vote for Jordan to speaker
is essentially a vote for Trump

00:10:03.334 --> 00:10:05.234
and his efforts
to overturn American democracy.

00:10:05.234 --> 00:10:07.734
Even if Jim Jordan is nominally
in charge of the House,

00:10:07.734 --> 00:10:09.267
he's just going to be
following Trump's orders.

00:10:09.267 --> 00:10:11.167
Trump is still the leader
of the Republican Party,

00:10:11.167 --> 00:10:12.601
and Jordan is fully
devoted to him.

00:10:12.601 --> 00:10:14.801
So I guess you could say
Jordan's the one who's...

00:10:14.801 --> 00:10:16.300
-Thirsty for leadership.

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:18.100
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:20.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

